From 1ff48cf810547d5b2dde9559f03b85c06675766d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamlesh Gurudasani <kamlesh@ti.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:59:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] libckteec: add PKCS#11 v3.2 ML-DSA and ML-KEM support

Add client-side support for the post-quantum mechanisms of the PKCS#11
TA: ML-DSA (FIPS 204) and ML-KEM (FIPS 203). libckteec is parameter-set
agnostic: the set is selected per key through CKA_PARAMETER_SET, so
ML-DSA-44/65/87 and ML-KEM-512/768/1024 are all served by this change.

- pkcs11.h: add the PKCS#11 v3.2 constants (CKM_ML_DSA*, CKM_ML_KEM*,
  CKK_ML_DSA/CKK_ML_KEM, CKA_PARAMETER_SET/SEED/ENCAPSULATE/DECAPSULATE
  and the *_TEMPLATE attributes, CKP_ML_*,
  CKR_PARAMETER_SET_NOT_SUPPORTED) and the PKCS#11 v3.0+ Interfaces
  types (CK_INTERFACE, CK_FUNCTION_LIST_3_0, CK_FUNCTION_LIST_3_2).
- pkcs11_ta.h: sync with the TA protocol header: new
  PKCS11_CMD_ENCAPSULATE_KEY/PKCS11_CMD_DECAPSULATE_KEY commands, the
  ML-DSA/ML-KEM mechanism, key type and attribute IDs,
  PKCS11_CKFM_ENCAPSULATE/DECAPSULATE, PKCS11_CKR_PARAMETER_SET_NOT_SUPPORTED,
  the EdDSA IDs, the OP-TEE vendor attribute flags and the TA version
  (1.2.0).
- pkcs11_api.c: implement C_EncapsulateKey()/C_DecapsulateKey() as
  ordinary exported C_* functions, plus C_GetInterfaceList() and
  C_GetInterface() returning a v3.2 function list. The KEM functions are
  not reachable through the legacy C_GetFunctionList() table, a known
  caveat for callers that only walk CK_FUNCTION_LIST. Members of the v3.x
  lists that libckteec does not implement are left NULL.
- pkcs11_processing.[ch]: add ck_encapsulate_key()/ck_decapsulate_key()
  which marshal the requests to the TA and unmarshal the resulting
  object handle and ciphertext.
- serialize_ck.c: accept the ML-DSA/ML-KEM mechanisms (no parameters) and
  handle CKA_PARAMETER_SET as a 32-bit value on the wire. Also fix
  deserialize_ck_attribute() which unconditionally read 4 bytes to widen
  a CK_ULONG-typed attribute, even when the TA reports a zero size (a
  valid "present but empty" state for an optional attribute). This
  fabricated a bogus value instead of reporting no value.

Tested against the PKCS#11 TA with ML-DSA and ML-KEM enabled: xtest -t
pkcs11 (0 failures), and on a TI AM62Lx EVM through OpenSSL's
pkcs11-provider (session and token key generation, sign/verify and
encapsulate/decapsulate for all six parameter sets).

Signed-off-by: Kamlesh Gurudasani <kamlesh@ti.com>
